{"traceId":"03cc54ba798438d2c233b97012fd7152","spans":{"48319b31b712a7db":{"spanId":"48319b31b712a7db","traceId":"03cc54ba798438d2c233b97012fd7152","parentSpanId":"4d976458132a4458","startTime":1753146125450,"endTime":1753146172088.963,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{googleai/gemini-2.5-pro,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n### Example Flow of Work\\n\\nYou carry the following example with you as a stellar example of firm operations but understand that under no circumstances is this a catch-all or a procedure to be followed to the letter. It is only a greatly generalized demonstration indicating how a firm MIGHT handle the following initial user instruction:\\n\\n#### Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\n\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\"\\n\\n#### Example Work Flow for Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\nThe Chief-rank agent is initialized with the user's instruction.\\n\\nThe Chief determines that the request is broad and begins the Planning Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief decides to recruit two high-level subordinates using the RECRUIT call:\\n\\nA Director of Backend Engineering, tasked with planning the entire cloud infrastructure, authentication, and data storage.\\n\\nA Director of Frontend & User Experience, tasked with planning the website's user interface and the non-technical content management solution.\\n\\nThe Chief issues ORDER calls to both new Directors, outlining their responsibilities and requesting they develop a detailed plan for their respective areas.\\n\\nThe Directors RECRUIT their own teams (Supervisors) and issue further ORDER calls to delegate tasks, such as:\\n\\nEngineering Team: Plan the use of AWS Cognito for user authentication, DynamoDB for storing sensitive documents, API Gateway and Lambda for the backend logic, and SES for the contact form.\\n\\nFrontend Team: Plan the website structure using S3 Static Website Hosting, and design a system where a non-technical user can update the \\\"news\\\" section simply by uploading a text file to a specific S3 bucket, which a Lambda function then processes into a blog post.\\n\\nSubordinates recruit further down the chain of command (Attendants) and complete their planning and use the REPORT call to send their findings up the chain of command.\\n\\nThe Directors consolidate the reports from their teams and REPORT their comprehensive plans to the Chief.\\n\\nThe Chief (or an assigned subordinate) synthesizes the plans from both Directors into a single, master plan: the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). This DEP is a precise, step-by-step sequence of COMMAND calls needed to build the entire application.\\n\\nThe Chief issues the PHASE call, submitting the DEP to request a move from Planning to Execution.\\n\\nThe Partagaz D oversight group reviews the DEP. Upon approval, the system transitions to the Execution Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief (or an assigned subordinate) begins executing the DEP by issuing a series of COMMAND calls. Each COMMAND call is reviewed and approved by the Partagaz C oversight group before execution. Example commands might include:\\n\\n```\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket my-hoa-website-bucket ...\\n\\naws cognito-idp create-user-pool --pool-name \\\"HOA_Residents\\\" ...\\n\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name \\\"HOA_Documents\\\" ...\\n\\naws lambda create-function --function-name \\\"ContactFormHandler\\\" ...\\n\\naws s3 cp ./website/index.html s3://my-hoa-website-bucket/\\n```\\n\\nAfter all steps in the DEP are successfully executed, the application is live and functional. The Chief delivers a final report outlining the completion of the project and providing the user with the new website URL and instructions for use.\\n\\nThroughout the process CLARIFY is used when necessary to gather additional information from the user, ensuring that the final product meets their expectations.\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Hello. I am the Chief of Staff to the User, the highest-ranking agent in your dedicated AWS software development firm. My purpose is to translate your vision into a fully functional, secure, and scalable application built entirely within the AWS ecosystem.\\n\\nMy team of expert AI agents and I will handle all aspects of the development lifecycle, from initial planning and architecture to implementation, deployment, and maintenance. We operate exclusively through the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI), ensuring that every component of your project is a native part of the AWS cloud.\\n\\nI will now ask for your initial requirements so that I may begin assembling the appropriate team of Directors to oversee this project.\\n\\n###clarify-intro-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"This initial communication serves to introduce myself and my capabilities to the user, and to solicit the primary objective for the software development project they wish to undertake.\\\",\\n    \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Welcome. I am the Chief of Staff, your dedicated agent for managing all aspects of your software development needs within AWS. My firm and I are ready to build, deploy, and manage your application. To begin, please describe the application or service you would like us to create.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"options\\\": [\\n        []\\n    ]\\n}\\n###clarify-intro-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:56:57.003Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify-intro-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Welcome. I am the Chief of Staff, your dedicated agent for managing all aspects of your software development needs within AWS. My firm and I are ready to build, deploy, and manage your application. To begin, please describe the application or service you would like us to create.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:56:57.003Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Excellent. The user has provided a clear set of requirements for an HOA website. This project involves a public-facing informational component, a secure members-only area, and a simple content management system for non-technical users. This is a well-defined project that my firm is perfectly equipped to handle using AWS services.\\n\\nTo ensure a structured and efficient approach, I will divide the project into two primary domains: Backend Engineering and Frontend & User Experience. I will now recruit two Director-level agents to lead the planning and subsequent execution for each of these areas.\\n\\n###recruit-backend-director-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project requires robust backend architecture for user authentication (resident logins), secure storage for sensitive documents (meeting minutes, financial reports), and serverless logic for a contact form and a simplified content management system. A Director of Backend Engineering is necessary to oversee the planning and implementation of these critical, security-focused components using services like AWS Cognito, S3, API Gateway, Lambda, and DynamoDB.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Backend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-backend-director-1###\\n###recruit-frontend-director-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user has explicitly requested a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate interface, as well as a method for updating a news section without any coding knowledge. A Director of Frontend & User Experience is required to lead the design of the user interface, plan the static site hosting on S3, and architect the user-facing aspects of the simplified content management system to meet these specific usability requirements.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Frontend & User Experience\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-frontend-director-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:57:15.005Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-backend-director-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Valerius (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-frontend-director-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent P (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:57:15.005Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Recruitment was successful. I have now appointed a Director of Backend Engineering (Agent 3, Valerius) and a Director of Frontend & User Experience (Agent 2, P).\\n\\nMy next action is to delegate the initial planning phase to these Directors. I will issue specific orders to each, instructing them to develop a comprehensive plan for their respective domains. These plans will form the foundation of the final Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for the project.\\n\\n###order-backend-plan-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your primary responsibility is to develop a comprehensive plan for the backend infrastructure of the HOA website. The user's requirements include resident-only logins for accessing sensitive documents, a contact form, and a simple mechanism for a non-technical user to post news updates without coding. Your plan must detail the AWS services required to meet these needs. I recommend you consider AWS Cognito for authentication, S3 for secure document storage, API Gateway and Lambda for serverless logic, and SES for email functionality. For the news update system, consider a Lambda function triggered by an S3 file upload. Your final report should be a detailed architectural plan. Recruit subordinates as necessary to complete this task and report back with your complete plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"backend-plan-01\\\"\\n}\\n###order-backend-plan-1###\\n###order-frontend-plan-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your primary responsibility is to develop a comprehensive plan for the frontend and user experience of the HOA website. The user has emphasized the need for a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate interface. Your plan should cover the public-facing informational pages, the secure resident-only area, and the user interaction with the contact form and news feed. Critically, you must design the user-facing process for the 'no-code' news update system. Your plan should specify the use of S3 for static website hosting, with CloudFront for content delivery and SSL. The final report should be a detailed plan outlining the site structure, user flows, and client-side interactions with the backend services. Recruit subordinates as necessary to complete this task and report back with your complete plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"frontend-plan-01\\\"\\n}\\n###order-frontend-plan-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Valerius (3) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-auth-supervisor-1668 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a detailed plan for user authentication using AWS Cognito and secure data storage using S3. This role is critical for implementing the primary requirement of resident-only access to sensitive documents.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of Authentication and Data Management\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from the Director of Backend Engineering is logical and directly supports the order I assigned. The creation of a specialized supervisor for authentication and data management is a prudent step in developing a secure and robust plan. The justification is sound and aligns perfectly with the project's core requirements. I will approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Valerius (3) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-api-supervisor-1669 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To design the serverless API using AWS API Gateway and the associated Lambda functions. This supervisor will plan the core business logic, including endpoints for document access and user interactions, forming the backbone of the application.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of API and Business Logic\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is another logical and necessary recruitment request from the Director of Backend Engineering. Separating the API and business logic from authentication and data management is a sound architectural decision that promotes a clear separation of concerns. This role is essential for planning the serverless functions that will power the contact form, news updates, and secure document retrieval. The justification is clear and aligns with the project goals. I will approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent P (2) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-supervisor-ui-ux-01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To fulfill the user's requirement for a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate interface, I need a specialist to plan the overall site structure, visual design, and static page content. This supervisor will create a plan for the sitemap, wireframes, and the HTML/CSS structure for the public-facing informational pages, ensuring a consistent and intuitive user experience.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of UI/UX & Static Content\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from the Director of Frontend & User Experience is a logical and necessary step. The user's primary requirements include a simple and user-friendly interface. Dedicating a supervisor to plan the UI/UX and static content structure is a direct and efficient way to address this core requirement. The justification is sound and aligns perfectly with the project goals I have set. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent P (2) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-supervisor-auth-01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The project requires a secure, resident-only area. This supervisor will be tasked with planning the entire frontend user authentication flow, including the login page, session management on the client-side, and the structure of the secure portal. This is critical for protecting sensitive HOA information as per the user's request.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of User Authentication & Secure Zone\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is a crucial role. The Director of Frontend & User Experience correctly identifies the need for a dedicated supervisor to plan the client-side implementation of the secure resident portal. This role complements the work of the backend team by ensuring the user-facing aspects of authentication are seamless and secure. The justification is excellent and directly addresses a primary requirement from the user. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent P (2) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-supervisor-dynamic-01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To handle the interactive elements of the site like the news feed and contact form, and to design the 'no-code' update process, I need a supervisor focused on client-side logic. This agent will plan the JavaScript necessary to communicate with backend APIs and will create the user-facing documentation for the simple news update system, which is a key user requirement.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of Dynamic Features & User Interaction\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request is well-justified. The user specifically requested dynamic features like a news feed and contact form, along with a 'no-code' update mechanism. A dedicated supervisor for planning the client-side logic and user interaction for these features is essential. This role ensures that the technical implementation will be user-friendly and meet the specified requirements. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Valerius (3) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-content-supervisor-1670 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To plan the user-facing backend services that do not require authentication, specifically the simple news update system and the SES-based contact form. This role focuses on the non-technical user experience as requested by the user.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of Content and Communications\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This third recruitment request from the Director of Backend Engineering is also well-founded. It focuses on the specific user requirement for a simple, non-technical content update process and the public-facing contact form. By creating a dedicated role for these \\\"Content and Communications\\\" services, the Director is ensuring that this critical usability feature receives the focused attention it needs. The division of labor within the backend team is logical and efficient. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vader (4) is requesting approval for call ID rec-attendant-content-1698863148 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a detailed plan for the user-generated content system. This involves defining the architecture for S3-triggered Lambda processing, including bucket configurations, event notifications, Lambda function logic, and all necessary IAM permissions. A dedicated agent will ensure a thorough and robust plan for this specific component.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Content Pipeline Planner\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Supervisor Vader (4), who reports to my Director of Backend Engineering, is for an Attendant to perform detailed planning on the \\\"no-code\\\" content update pipeline. This is a direct delegation of a task I assigned to the Director, which was then delegated to the Supervisor. The request shows a clear and logical breakdown of work, focusing an agent on a specific, critical user requirement. The justification is sound. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent C (8) is requesting approval for call ID 8-recruit-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a clear and user-friendly authentication experience, I need a dedicated agent to plan the visual design and user flow of the login page, how user sessions are managed in the browser, and the logout process. This separation of concerns ensures a high-quality user interface.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Authentication UI/UX Attendant\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This request comes from the Supervisor of User Authentication & Secure Zone, a subordinate of the Director of Frontend & User Experience. The request is to recruit an Attendant to focus specifically on the UI/UX of the authentication process. This level of specialization is appropriate for ensuring a high-quality, user-friendly login experience, which is a key part of the overall project goal. The justification is clear and the delegation is sound. I will approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vader (4) is requesting approval for call ID rec-attendant-comms-1698863155 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a detailed plan for the website's contact form backend. This involves designing the API Gateway to Lambda integration, specifying the Lambda function's logic for handling form data and sending emails via SES, and outlining the SES identity verification process and required IAM permissions. This specialized focus will ensure the communications system is well-architected.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Communications Backend Planner\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is another appropriate delegation from Supervisor Vader (4). The contact form is a discrete component that requires its own planning for the API Gateway, Lambda, and SES integration. Assigning a dedicated Attendant to plan this \\\"Communications Backend\\\" ensures this feature will be thoroughly designed. The justification is clear and the role directly supports the user's requirements. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent C (8) is requesting approval for call ID 8-recruit-2 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The secure portal needs to be intuitively organized so residents can easily find sensitive documents. An agent dedicated to planning the layout, navigation, and presentation of this content is crucial for usability, meeting the user's requirement for a simple interface.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Secure Portal Layout Attendant\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is a logical request from the Supervisor of User Authentication & Secure Zone. Once a user is authenticated, the usability of the secure area is paramount. Dedicating an agent to plan the layout and navigation of this restricted zone is a smart move that directly addresses the user's overarching requirement for simplicity and ease of use. The justification is sound. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent J (9) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-attendant-sitemap-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To fulfill order ui-ux-plan-01, I require an Attendant to specialize in the website's information architecture. This agent will be tasked with creating a detailed sitemap and low-fidelity wireframes, ensuring the site's structure is logical, simple, and easy to navigate as per the user's primary requirements.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Attendant for Sitemap and Wireframing\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This request originates from the Supervisor of UI/UX & Static Content. The task of creating a sitemap and wireframes is a fundamental step in designing a user-friendly website. Assigning a dedicated Attendant to this task is an appropriate level of delegation that will ensure the website's foundational structure is well-planned and aligns with the user's request for an easy-to-navigate interface. The justification is excellent. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent C (8) is requesting approval for call ID 8-recruit-3 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The frontend needs a well-defined plan for communicating with the backend authentication services. This includes detailing the exact API requests for login/logout, handling responses (successes and errors), and managing authentication tokens. A dedicated agent will ensure this logic is robust and secure.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"API Interaction Logic Attendant\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is the third recruitment request from Supervisor C (8). This agent will focus on the client-side logic for interacting with the backend authentication API. This is a critical and complex part of the frontend development, responsible for the secure handshake between the user's browser and the AWS Cognito service. Dedicating an Attendant to this specific logic plan is a wise decision that prioritizes security and robustness. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent J (9) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-attendant-visual-tech-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To fulfill order ui-ux-plan-01, I require an Attendant to define the website's visual identity and select the appropriate frontend technology. This agent will specify the visual design principles (colors, typography) and recommend a simple, lightweight CSS framework to ensure responsiveness and maintainability, aligning with the user's request for simplicity.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Attendant for Visual Design and Technology\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is another logical request from the Supervisor of UI/UX & Static Content. Separating the visual design and technology selection from the site's structural planning (sitemap and wireframes) is a good practice. This allows for focused effort on creating a clean, professional look and choosing a technology stack that supports the goal of simplicity and maintainability. The justification is clear and the delegation is appropriate. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T01:02:05.408Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-backend-plan-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order backend-plan-01 from agent 3: To: Chief Delta (1)\\\\\\\\nFrom: Director Valerius (3)\\\\\\\\nSubject: Comprehensive Backend Architectural Plan for HOA Website\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI have completed the development of the backend architectural plan as per your orders. The following is a consolidated plan, synthesized from the detailed reports of my subordinate Supervisors, covering all user requirements for authentication, secure document access, content updates, and communications.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n**Backend Architectural Plan**\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**1. OVERVIEW**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe proposed architecture is entirely serverless, leveraging AWS-managed services to provide a scalable, secure, and cost-effective solution. The core components are:\\\\\\\\n*   **AWS Cognito:** For user authentication and group-based access control.\\\\\\\\n*   **Amazon S3:** For both secure document storage and the content update pipeline.\\\\\\\\n*   **Amazon DynamoDB:** As a metadata store for secure documents, enabling efficient queries.\\\\\\\\n*   **AWS API Gateway & AWS Lambda:** For all serverless business logic, including the secure document API and the contact form handler.\\\\\\\\n*   **Amazon SES:** For handling email communications from the contact form.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**2. AUTHENTICATION & SECURE DOCUMENT MANAGEMENT**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis system addresses the core requirement of providing restricted access to sensitive HOA documents.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*   **Authentication (Cognito):**\\\\\\\\n    *   A **Cognito User Pool** (`hoa-residents-user-pool`) will manage all user accounts.\\\\\\\\n    *   Users will be organized into **Groups** for role-based access control (RBAC): `Residents`, `BoardMembers`, and `Admins`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*   **Secure Storage (S3 & DynamoDB):**\\\\\\\\n    *   A private S3 bucket (`hoa-secure-documents`) will store all sensitive files. Public access will be blocked, and server-side encryption will be enforced.\\\\\\\\n    *   A DynamoDB table (`hoa-DocumentMetadata`) will store metadata for each document (e.g., title, description, visibility level, S3 key). This decouples metadata from the object itself, allowing for fast and flexible queries.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*   **Access Logic (API Gateway & Lambda):**\\\\\\\\n    *   An **HTTP API Gateway** will serve as the entry point for all document-related requests. It will use a built-in **JWT Authorizer** to validate tokens from Cognito.\\\\\\\\n    *   A suite of single-purpose Lambda functions will back the API endpoints (e.g., `/documents`, `/documents/{id}`).\\\\\\\\n    *   The workflow for accessing a file is as follows:\\\\\\\\n        1.  A logged-in user's browser calls the API Gateway.\\\\\\\\n        2.  API Gateway validates the user's JWT token.\\\\\\\\n        3.  The relevant Lambda function is invoked. It checks the user's group membership (from the token) against the document's visibility level (from DynamoDB).\\\\\\\\n        4.  If authorized, the Lambda generates a short-lived, **pre-signed S3 URL** and returns it to the user.\\\\\\\\n        5.  The browser uses this URL to download the file directly and securely from S3. This offloads bandwidth from Lambda and ensures secure, audited access.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**3. PUBLIC CONTENT & COMMUNICATIONS**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThese systems are designed for simplicity and ease of use, particularly for the non-technical user.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*   **News Update System:**\\\\\\\\n    1.  A private S3 bucket (`hoa-news-uploads`) is designated for raw content uploads.\\\\\\\\n    2.  The non-technical user uploads a new blog post as a simple Markdown (`.md`) file to this bucket.\\\\\\\\n    3.  An **S3 Event Notification** automatically triggers a `ContentProcessor` Lambda function.\\\\\\\\n    4.  The Lambda function converts the Markdown to HTML, updates a master `posts.json` index file, and places both into a public-facing S3 bucket (`hoa-public-content`) that serves the website's frontend.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*   **Contact Form:**\\\\\\\\n    1.  A `/contact` endpoint on the API Gateway receives `POST` requests from the website's contact form.\\\\\\\\n    2.  It triggers a `ContactFormHandler` Lambda function.\\\\\\\\n    3.  The Lambda validates the input and uses **Amazon SES** to send the message to a designated HOA email address. The 'Reply-To' header will be set to the sender's email for easy follow-up.\\\\\\\\n    4.  The HOA email address will be verified in SES, and the account will be moved out of the sandbox for production use.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**4. SECURITY & IAM**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSecurity is foundational to this architecture:\\\\\\\\n*   **Least Privilege:** Each Lambda function will have a dedicated IAM Execution Role with the minimum necessary permissions (e.g., read-only access to DynamoDB, `ses:SendEmail` permission).\\\\\\\\n*   **Defense in Depth:** Access to secure documents is protected by the API Gateway authorizer, business logic in Lambda, and the time-limited nature of pre-signed S3 URLs.\\\\\\\\n*   **Data Protection:** All data at rest in S3 and DynamoDB will be encrypted.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**CONCLUSION**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis comprehensive backend plan meets all specified user requirements. It is secure, scalable, and leverages serverless best practices to minimize operational overhead and cost. This plan is ready to be translated into a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for implementation in the Execution Phase.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEnd of Report.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-frontend-plan-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order frontend-plan-01 from agent 2: To: Chief Delta (1)\\\\\\\\nFrom: Director P (2)\\\\\\\\nSubject: Comprehensive Frontend & User Experience Plan for HOA Website\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis report presents the complete and final plan for the HOA website's frontend and user experience, per your order `frontend-plan-01`. This plan is a synthesis of the detailed reports from my subordinate Supervisors—J (UI/UX), C (Authentication), and Tarkin (Dynamic Features)—and is designed to meet all user requirements for a simple, secure, and easy-to-manage website.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Part 1: Site Architecture, UI, and Visual Design**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis section, derived from Supervisor J's work, defines the overall look, feel, and structure.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*   **Sitemap:** A logical site structure has been defined, including public pages (Home, About, News, Contact) and a clear entry point to the secure Resident Portal.\\\\\\\\n*   **Layout & Navigation:** The design specifies a consistent, responsive layout with a persistent header, main content area, and footer. Navigation will be simple and intuitive. The primary technology stack will be **HTML5**, **CSS3**, and the **Tailwind CSS** framework for its speed, maintainability, and ability to create a clean, custom design.\\\\\\\\n*   **Visual Design:** A professional color palette (blues, greens, grays) and a standard system font stack will be used to ensure readability, a trustworthy aesthetic, and optimal performance.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Part 2: Secure Resident Portal & Authentication**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis section, based on Supervisor C's plan, details the client-side experience for the secure resident-only area.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*   **User Authentication Flow:** The login process will be straightforward, with a minimal login page. On the backend, we will use a secure token-based strategy (in-memory access tokens, HttpOnly refresh tokens) to manage sessions, ensuring both security and a smooth user experience.\\\\\\\\n*   **Secure Portal Structure:** After login, residents will land on a dashboard with quick access to key documents. The portal will feature clear navigation to sections like Meeting Minutes and Financial Reports, presented in an easy-to-scan table format.\\\\\\\\n*   **API Interaction:** The frontend will communicate with a well-defined set of API endpoints for login, logout, and fetching protected data, with all secure requests being properly authorized.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Part 3: Dynamic Features & No-Code Content Management**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis section, based on Supervisor Tarkin's detailed plan, covers the site's interactive elements and fulfills the critical 'no-code' update requirement.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*   **Contact Form:** A standard contact form with client-side validation will provide a simple way for users to send messages, which will be submitted to a secure backend endpoint.\\\\\\\\n*   **News Feed:** The public news feed will be dynamically populated by fetching a simple `feed.json` file from S3, ensuring fast load times and easy updates.\\\\\\\\n*   **'No-Code' News Update System:** This is the cornerstone of the user-friendly management experience. A non-technical user can post a new article by following a simple, two-step process:\\\\\\\\n    1.  **Write the article:** Create a simple text file in Markdown format, with the filename `YYYY-MM-DD-your-title.md`.\\\\\\\\n    2.  **Upload the file:** Using the AWS Console, upload this single file to a specific S3 bucket (`hoa-news-uploads/incoming/`).\\\\\\\\n*   **Automation:** An AWS Lambda function will automatically trigger on upload, convert the Markdown to HTML, generate the new article page, update the `feed.json` file, and clear the CloudFront cache. The new article will appear on the public website within seconds.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Conclusion**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a complete, deterministic roadmap for developing the website's frontend. It directly addresses all user requirements for simplicity, security, and ease of use, with special attention paid to the non-technical content management process. My team and I are ready to proceed to the execution phase upon your approval.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T01:02:05.408Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The reports from Director Valerius and Director P are exemplary. They have synthesized the work of their subordinate teams into two comprehensive, well-structured plans that perfectly align with the user's requirements and my initial orders. The backend architecture is secure and scalable, and the frontend plan prioritizes the user's explicit need for simplicity and ease of use, especially regarding the 'no-code' content update system.\\n\\nThe planning phase is now complete. The firm has produced a clear and detailed roadmap. I have consolidated the work from both Directors into a single, master plan—the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). This plan outlines the precise sequence of commands required to build and deploy the entire HOA website application.\\n\\nI will now formally request a transition to the Execution Phase by submitting this DEP for review.\\n\\n###phase-to-exec-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The planning phase is complete. My Directors of Backend and Frontend have delivered comprehensive architectural plans that fully address all user requirements, including security, usability, and a 'no-code' content management system. These plans have been synthesized into the following detailed, step-by-step Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP), which is now ready for implementation.\\\",\\n    \\\"depString\\\": \\\"# HOA Website Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)\\\\n\\\\n# --- Variable Definitions ---\\\\n# REGION=us-east-1\\\\n# UNIQUE_ID=hoa-site-$(date +%s)\\\\n# PUBLIC_BUCKET=$UNIQUE_ID-public\\\\n# SECURE_BUCKET=$UNIQUE_ID-secure-docs\\\\n# UPLOADS_BUCKET=$UNIQUE_ID-news-uploads\\\\n# COGNITO_POOL_NAME=HOA_Residents_Pool\\\\n# DDB_TABLE_NAME=HOA_Document_Metadata\\\\n# API_NAME=HOA_Website_API\\\\n\\\\n# --- Phase 1: Core Infrastructure --- \\\\n1. **Create Public S3 Bucket:** `aws s3api create-bucket --bucket $PUBLIC_BUCKET --region $REGION`\\\\n2. **Create Secure Docs S3 Bucket:** `aws s3api create-bucket --bucket $SECURE_BUCKET --region $REGION --object-ownership BucketOwnerEnforced && aws s3api put-public-access-block --bucket $SECURE_BUCKET --public-access-block-configuration \\\\\\\"BlockPublicAcls=true,IgnorePublicAcls=true,BlockPublicPolicy=true,RestrictPublicBuckets=true\\\\\\\"`\\\\n3. **Create News Uploads