otification-configuration --bucket $UPLOADS_BUCKET --notification-configuration '{\\\\\\\"LambdaFunctionConfigurations\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"LambdaFunctionArn\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"<CONTENT_PROCESSOR_LAMBDA_ARN>\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Events\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"s3:ObjectCreated:*\\\\\\\"]}]}'`\\\\n\\\\n# --- Phase 5: Frontend Deployment --- \\\\n24. **Create index.html:** `echo \\\\\\\"<h1>Welcome to the HOA Website</h1><a href='/news'>News</a><a href='/login.html'>Resident Login</a>\\\\\\\" > index.html`\\\\n25. **Upload index.html:** `aws s3 cp index.html s3://$PUBLIC_BUCKET/`\\\\n26. **Create login.html:** `echo \\\\\\\"<h2>Resident Login</h2><form><!-- Login Form --></form>\\\\\\\" > login.html`\\\\n27. **Upload login.html:** `aws s3 cp login.html s3://$PUBLIC_BUCKET/`\\\\n28. **Enable Static Website Hosting:** `aws s3 website s3://$PUBLIC_BUCKET/ --index-document index.html`\\\\n\\\\n# --- Phase 6: CDN & Finalization --- \\\\n29. **Create CloudFront Distribution:** `aws cloudfront create-distribution --origin-domain-name $PUBLIC_BUCKET.s3-website-$REGION.amazonaws.com --default-root-object index.html`\\\\n\\\\n# --- Phase 7: Manual User Actions --- \\\\n30. **User Action:** Verify email address in SES for sending contact form emails.\\\\n31. **User Action:** Request production access for SES to move out of the sandbox.\\\"\\n}\\n###phase-to-exec-1###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"custom\":{}}],\"custom\":{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"The reports from Director Valerius and Director P are exemplary. They have synthesized the work of their subordinate teams into two comprehensive, well-structured plans that perfectly align with the user's requirements and my initial orders. The backend architecture is secure and scalable, and the frontend plan prioritizes the user's explicit need for simplicity and ease of use, especially regarding the 'no-code' content update system.\\n\\nThe planning phase is now complete. The firm has produced a clear and detailed roadma